    "result_text": "The build passes and the single acceptance test is green. The log confirms the consolidated path working: `Duplicate owner identityKey at POST /api/owners: +61400000004||` \u2014 a whole-key match rejected with 409.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**`identityKey` definition** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId` (null email/householdId \u2192 empty segment).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 Replaced the three separate checks (`rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, and the household opt-in rejection in `applyHousehold`) with one `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` that throws only when a new owner's *whole* `identityKey` equals an existing owner's. `applyHousehold` now still assigns the shared `householdId` to household members (same lastName+address) but no longer rejects \u2014 so two members of one household (same `householdId`) with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed. Removed the now-dead `toComparableTelephone` helper and stale imports.\n\n2. **New `DuplicateIdentityException`** + a handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** returning **409** with `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`. Removed the three obsolete exception classes (`DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`) and their handlers.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `identityKey` string property to the `Owner` schema so it's returned in the response.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 Populates `identityKey` on the DTO via the same derivation.\n\n**Behavioural change (as specified):** the former per-telephone, per-email, and household duplicate rules no longer fire independently; only an exact full-key collision is a 409.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the old `sharesHousehold` request flag is now inert \u2014 it previously gated the household rejection, which the spec folds into the identity key, so nothing reads it anymore. I left the field in the API for compatibility rather than removing it.",
